## ============================================================
## SCRIPT 2 — VAR2CSA / Cumulative antibodies as outcomes
## ALIGNED WITH THE ANTIGEN SCRIPTS
##
## WHY NO LEFT CENSORING HERE
##   In the antigen scripts the antigen is the OUTCOME, so a value
##   below the LLOQ can be handled as an interval and survreg uses
##   it properly. Here the antigen is a PREDICTOR, and censoring a
##   predictor is a different and much harder problem; survreg only
##   censors the response.
##
##   But the issue does not disappear: sub-LLOQ concentrations are
##   still entering the model as if they were reliable measurements,
##   when below that limit the interpolated value is blank noise
##   pushed through the standard curve. The standard treatment for a
##   censored PREDICTOR is substitution at LLOQ/sqrt(2), which is
##   what SUB_BELOW_LLOQ does. Set it to FALSE to keep the previous
##   behaviour and compare.
##
## WHAT IS NOW THE SAME AS THE ANTIGEN SCRIPTS
##   - automated LRT screening of HIV x predictor and gestweeks x
##     predictor; the predictor x gravidity x site term is retained
##     a priori because it is the primary hypothesis
##   - cubic-spline refit of the selected structure, with an AIC
##     comparison against the linear form (reviewer point 6)
##   - SIMULTANEOUS 95% confidence bands across the predictor curve
##     instead of 200 pointwise intervals (reviewer point 5)
##   - common support as a switch: restrict the prediction grid, not
##     necessarily the data
##   - within-site gravidity contrasts available (reviewer point 7)
##   - aliased coefficients excluded from every contrast
##   - net and fumig left as the recoding script delivers them,
##     where 999 was already merged into "yes"
## ============================================================

